From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 15:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: dw9719: make sure the lens holds the position
 after resume

dw9719_resume() ramps the lens to the focus control's value in steps of
DW9719_CTRL_STEPS, 1 ms apart. On the OnePlus Pad 4's DW9800K, in its
smart actuator control (SAC) mode, the position register then read 434
(0x01b2) while the control and the last write were 450: the chip had
not taken the final position, which came while it still moved the lens
to the step before. The lens stays one step short until user space
writes the control again.

Read the position register back after the ramp and, while it differs,
write the position again 2 ms later, up to 15 times. A chip that takes
the last write costs one register read. A position that is never taken
only logs a warning: the lens is merely out of focus.

Signed-off-by: mzak <mzak.amin@gmail.com>
Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c | 41 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 41 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
index b4bf9178370e..7be9b8524f48 100644
--- a/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
+++ b/drivers/media/i2c/dw9719.c
@@ -22,6 +22,8 @@
 #define DW9719_MAX_FOCUS_POS	1023
 #define DW9719_CTRL_STEPS	16
 #define DW9719_CTRL_DELAY_US	1000
+#define DW9719_SETTLE_TRIES	15
+#define DW9719_SETTLE_US	2000
 
 #define DW9718S_PD			CCI_REG8(0)
 
@@ -258,6 +260,41 @@ static int dw9719_t_focus_abs(struct dw9719_device *dw9719, s32 value)
 	return ret;
 }
 
+/*
+ * A position written while the actuator still moves the lens to the one
+ * before may not be taken: on a DW9800K in its smart actuator control (SAC)
+ * mode the position register read one step short of the control's value
+ * after the resume ramp, whose writes are 1 ms apart. Read the register
+ * back and write the position again until the chip holds it.
+ */
+static int dw9719_settle(struct dw9719_device *dw9719, int pos)
+{
+	u32 reg = dw9719->model == DW9718S ? DW9718S_VCM_CURRENT
+					   : DW9719_VCM_CURRENT;
+	u64 val;
+	int ret;
+	int i;
+
+	for (i = 0; ; i++) {
+		ret = cci_read(dw9719->regmap, reg, &val, NULL);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+		if (val == (u64)pos)
+			return 0;
+		if (i == DW9719_SETTLE_TRIES)
+			break;
+
+		fsleep(DW9719_SETTLE_US);
+		ret = dw9719_t_focus_abs(dw9719, pos);
+		if (ret)
+			return ret;
+	}
+
+	dev_warn(dw9719->dev, "lens position %d not taken: the chip holds %llu\n",
+		 pos, val);
+	return 0;
+}
+
 static int dw9719_set_ctrl(struct v4l2_ctrl *ctrl)
 {
 	struct dw9719_device *dw9719 = container_of(ctrl->handler,
@@ -325,6 +362,10 @@ static int dw9719_resume(struct device *dev)
 		usleep_range(DW9719_CTRL_DELAY_US, DW9719_CTRL_DELAY_US + 10);
 	}
 
+	ret = dw9719_settle(dw9719, current_focus);
+	if (ret)
+		goto err_power_down;
+
 	return 0;
 
 err_power_down:
-- 
2.43.0

